From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 19:08:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: run a looping vertex stage that writes memory as
 compute

An Apple GPU kills a Metal vertex function invocation that runs for
longer than about 10 ms and reports a timeout; what the invocation had
not yet done is lost. The limit is per invocation: a million short
vertices in one 200 ms draw are not killed, a one-thread compute
dispatch runs 700 ms and a fragment invocation 90 ms, on an Apple7 GPU
under macOS 27.0.1.

KHR-GLES31.core.texture_cube_map_array.image_op_vertex_sh and
image_op_tessellation_evaluation_sh run one invocation that copies a
whole cube map array image texel by texel and land just past the
limit. Without validation the kill comes after the copy and the cases
pass; under Metal validation, or on a busy GPU, the copy is cut short
and the queue faults.

As KK_WORKAROUND_21, the stage that would be the Metal vertex function,
the vertex shader or a tessellation pipeline's evaluation shader, runs
as compute through the transform feedback pass-through with nothing to
capture when it writes memory anywhere and contains a loop. A store
free stage that loops past the limit loses only its draw's rasterized
output, which no realistic shader approaches; routing every looping
stage would put ordinary shaders on the slower path. Geometry shader
and transform feedback pipelines already run the stage as compute.

The routed draws of one pass do not wait for each other, as Metal
vertex functions do not, and pin no geometry heap: a barrier before
each draw's dispatch cost about 5 us per draw, and the heap reset a
command buffer of its own per pass. About 0.12 ms per pass segment,
0.3 us per draw and 1 ns per vertex remain on an M1 Ultra.

kosmickrisp_vertex_compute_routing checks the decision.
kosmickrisp_long_vertex_invocation runs a 50 ms vertex and a 100 ms
tessellation evaluation invocation to completion, and with
MESA_KK_DISABLE_WORKAROUNDS=21 its --expect-loss mode shows them cut
short. kosmickrisp_vertex_compute_draws checks the stores and tiles of
64 routed draws in one pass. MESA_KK_DEBUG=vertex_compute reports each
stage the workaround routes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
